#DESCRIPTION
Intrinsic magnetic field: static dipole.

The evolved field is switched off (SOLVEEM F) and UNIFORMSTATE carries zero
field, so the only magnetic field in the domain is the frozen intrinsic field
B0 declared by DIPOLE. The plot output can then be compared point by point
with the analytic dipole, and any leakage of B0 into the evolved field, or any
failure to add it to the total field, shows up immediately.

Output unit is 'planet', so B0x/B0y/B0z come out in nT and X/Y in planetary
radii (PLANETRADIUS = lNormSI here, so one code unit is one planetary radius).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-4.0                    xMin   [code units: 1 unit = 1 planetary radius]
 4.0                    xMax
-4.0                    yMin
 4.0                    yMax
-2.0                    zMin   four cells so that z = 0 is a node
 2.0                    zMax   plane and the body fits inside   'z=0' cut is then the exact z = 0 plane

#NCELL
32                      nCellX
32                      nCellY
4                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
16                      maxBlockSizeY
4                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

No field solve: B1 stays at its initial value (zero) and E stays zero, so the
only field acting on the particles is the intrinsic one.
#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
F                       useHybridPIC

#PLASMA
2                       nS
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge
0.04                    mass           Species 1: electrons
-1.0                    charge

Zero background field: B1 = 0 and E = 0. The plasma only drifts so that the
test particles have a mean velocity whose rotation can be measured.
#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions
0.0                     ux [km/s]
20.0                    uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
1.0e4                   T [K]
0.2                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 1: electrons (n_e = n_i)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
20.0                    uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
1.0e4                   T [K]
0.0                     bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

The planetary radius is the reference radius of the dipole (rRef < 0 below),
and one code length unit is one planetary radius.
#PLANETRADIUS
1.0e5                   radius [m]

Equatorial field strength 100 nT on the reference sphere r = 1, axis tilted
30 degrees from +z towards -x (the BATSRUS sense for phi = 0).
#DIPOLE
100.0                   strength [nT]
30.0                    theta [deg]
0.0                     phi [deg]
-1.0                    rRef [m, <0 = take it from the body/planet radius]

#TIMESTEPPING
F                       useFixedDt
0.2                     cfl

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI [m]
1.0e5                   uNormSI [m/s]

#MONITOR
10                      dnReport

#PARTICLES
2                       npcelx
2                       npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii planet    plotString
-1                      dn
10.0                    dt
1                       dx
B0x B0y B0z Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez   plotVar

#PARTICLETRACKER
T                       usePT

#TPPARTICLES
2                       particles per cell in X
2                       particles per cell in Y
1                       particles per cell in Z

#TPREGION
uniform                 region

#TPCELLINTERVAL
8                       nIntervalX
8                       nIntervalY
1                       nIntervalZ

#TPSAVE
0                       iSpecies
planet                  IOUnit
10                      dnSave
0.5                     launchThreshold

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
10.0                    TimeMax

#RUN
